Cert-Yjs
========

Cert-Yjs is written after three implementations of the Yjs CRDT: Yjs
(https://github.com/yjs/yjs, Kevin Jahns and contributors), yrs
(https://github.com/y-crdt/y-crdt, Bartosz Sypytkowski and contributors) and
y-octo (https://github.com/y-crdt/y-octo, the Toeverything / AFFiNE team), all
under the MIT License.

This product includes software derived from y-octo: the Go data structures and
the integrate algorithm in yjs/ are a port of y-octo's `src/doc` (in particular
`store.rs` and `codec/`). y-octo's license is reproduced below as it requires.

The text observer (yjs/observe.go) follows Yjs's YTextEvent.delta
classification (src/utils/YEvent.js), so Yjs's license is reproduced below as
well. No code is ported from yrs; its notice is added here when that happens.

